    ## ```
    weave filter_values_range with lo as V, hi as V into map of K to V:
        var out as map of K to V is map of K to V
        for k in essence of self:
            var v as V is self at k
            if v >= lo and v <= hi:
                calling out.put with k, v
        return out

# --- Generic ordering: K: Ordered, V: Ordered ------------------------------

enchanting map of shard K to shard V where K: Ordered, V: Par:
    ## New list with the keys sorted ascending through `calling K.cmp`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is the map to read.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned `list of K` sorted ascending with the `Ordered` bind of `K`. Works for any `K` that implements `Ordered` (`int`, `float`, `string`, a bound `seal`/`rune`, ...). Borrows the receiver.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var ks as list of string is calling m.keys_sorted
    ## calling ks at 0    # "alpha"
    ## ```
    weave keys_sorted into list of K:
        var ks as list of K is list of K
        for k in essence of self:
            calling ks.push with k
        var n as int is calling ks.len
        var i as int is 1
        while i < n:
            var key as K is ks at i
            var j as int is i - 1
            var moving as bool is j >= 0
            while moving:
                var left as K is ks at j
                var c as int is calling left.cmp with key
                if c > 0:
                    set ks at (j + 1) is left
                    set j is j - 1
                    set moving is j >= 0
                else:
                    set moving is false
            set ks at (j + 1) is key
            set i is i + 1
        return ks

enchanting map of shard K to shard V where K: Par, V: Ordered:
    ## New list with the values sorted ascending through `calling V.cmp`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - None: the receiver is the map to read.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned `list of V` sorted ascending with the `Ordered` bind of `V`. Works for `int`, `float`, `string` and bound `seal`/`rune` values. Borrows the receiver.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var vs as list of string is calling m.values_sorted
    ## calling vs at 0    # "dos"
    ## ```
    weave values_sorted into list of V:
        var vs as list of V is list of V
        for k in essence of self:
            var v as V is self at k
            calling vs.push with v
        var n as int is calling vs.len
        var i as int is 1
        while i < n:
            var key as V is vs at i
            var j as int is i - 1
            var moving as bool is j >= 0
            while moving:
                var left as V is vs at j
                var c as int is calling left.cmp with key
                if c > 0:
                    set vs at (j + 1) is left
                    set j is j - 1
                    set moving is j >= 0
                else:
                    set moving is false
            set vs at (j + 1) is key
            set i is i + 1
        return vs

