## New list with the keys of `m` sorted ascending.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the map to read. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `list of K` sorted with the `Ordered` bind of `K`; unlike the 0.15.0 version it also works when `K` is `string`. Borrows `m`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var ks as list of string is calling keys_sorted_of with m
## calling ks at 0    # "alpha"
## ```
weave keys_sorted_of shard K and V where K: Ordered, V: Par with m as map of K to V into list of K:
    var ks as list of K is list of K
    for k in m:
        calling ks.push with k
    var n as int is calling ks.len
    var i as int is 1
    while i < n:
        var key as K is ks at i
        var j as int is i - 1
        var moving as bool is j >= 0
        while moving:
            var left as K is ks at j
            var c as int is calling left.cmp with key
            if c > 0:
                set ks at (j + 1) is left
                set j is j - 1
                set moving is j >= 0
            else:
                set moving is false
        set ks at (j + 1) is key
        set i is i + 1
    return ks

## New list with the values of `m` sorted ascending.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the map to read. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `list of V` sorted with the `Ordered` bind of `V`, so it also works when `V` is `string`. Borrows `m`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var vs as list of int is calling values_sorted_of with m
## ```
weave values_sorted_of shard K and V where K: Par, V: Ordered with m as map of K to V into list of V:
    var vs as list of V is list of V
    for k in m:
        var v as V is m at k
        calling vs.push with v
    var n as int is calling vs.len
    var i as int is 1
    while i < n:
        var key as V is vs at i
        var j as int is i - 1
        var moving as bool is j >= 0
        while moving:
            var left as V is vs at j
            var c as int is calling left.cmp with key
            if c > 0:
                set vs at (j + 1) is left
                set j is j - 1
                set moving is j >= 0
            else:
                set moving is false
        set vs at (j + 1) is key
        set i is i + 1
    return vs

## Combines `a` and `b` into a new map; `b` wins on collision.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `a`: the left map. Read only.
## - `b`: the right map. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `map of K to V` the caller releases with `banish`. Borrows both maps.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var m as map of string to int is calling map_merge with a, b
## ```
weave map_merge shard K and V where K: Par, V: Par with a as map of K to V, b as map of K to V into map of K to V:
    var out as map of K to V is map of K to V
    for k in a:
        var v as V is a at k
        calling out.put with k, v
    for k in b:
        var v as V is b at k
        calling out.put with k, v
    return out

## Combines `a` and `b` into a new map; keys of `a` keep their value.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `a`: the left map, whose values win. Read only.
## - `b`: the right map. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `map of K to V` the caller releases with `banish`. Borrows both maps.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var m as map of string to int is calling map_merge_keep_left with a, b
## ```
weave map_merge_keep_left shard K and V where K: Par, V: Par with a as map of K to V, b as map of K to V into map of K to V:
    var out as map of K to V is map of K to V
    for k in a:
        var v as V is a at k
        calling out.put with k, v
    for k in b:
        if not (calling out.contains with k):
            var v as V is b at k
            calling out.put with k, v
    return out

## Combines every map of `maps` into one; later maps win.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `maps`: the maps to merge in order. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `map of K to V` the caller releases with `banish`. Borrows `maps`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var m as map of string to int is calling map_merge_all with maps
## ```
weave map_merge_all shard K and V where K: Par, V: Par with maps as list of map of K to V into map of K to V:
    var out as map of K to V is map of K to V
    for m in maps:
        for k in m:
            var v as V is m at k
            calling out.put with k, v
    return out

## Builds a map from the parallel lists `ks` and `vs`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `ks`: the keys, consumed up to `min(ks.len, vs.len)`. Read only.
## - `vs`: the values. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `map of K to V` with `min(ks.len, vs.len)` entries; later duplicate keys overwrite earlier ones. Borrows both lists.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var m as map of string to int is calling map_from_lists with ks, vs
## ```
weave map_from_lists shard K and V where K: Par, V: Par with ks as list of K, vs as list of V into map of K to V:
    var out as map of K to V is map of K to V
    var limit as int is calling ks.len
    if (calling vs.len) < limit:
        set limit is calling vs.len
    var i as int is 0
    while i < limit:
        var k as K is ks at i
        var v as V is vs at i
        calling out.put with k, v
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Builds a map from a list of `oracle.Pair`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `ps`: the key/value pairs to insert in order. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `map of K to V`; later duplicate keys overwrite earlier ones. Borrows `ps`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var m as map of string to int is calling from_pairs with ps
## ```
weave from_pairs shard K and V where K: Par, V: Par with ps as list of oracle.Pair of K and V into map of K to V:
    var out as map of K to V is map of K to V
    for p in ps:
        calling out.put with p.first, p.second
    return out

## Submap of `m` with the entries whose `string` value contains `sub`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the map to filter. Read only.
## - `sub`: the substring to look for inside each value.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `map of K to string`. Unlike the method form, the module function infers `K` from its argument, so it works for any key type without a concrete block. Borrows `m`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var f as map of int to string is calling map_filter_values_contains with m, "un"
## ```
weave map_filter_values_contains shard K where K: Par with m as map of K to string, sub as string into map of K to string:
    var out as map of K to string is map of K to string
    for k in m:
        var v as string is m at k
        if calling v.contains with sub:
            calling out.put with k, v
    return out


