## Builds an `map of string to bool` from the parallel lists `ks` and `vs`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `ks`: the keys, read up to `min(ks.len, vs.len)`. Read only.
## - `vs`: the values. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned `map of string to bool` the caller releases with `banish`. Borrows both lists.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var m as map of string to bool is calling atlas.from_lists_sb with ks, vs
## ```
weave from_lists_sb with ks as list of string, vs as list of bool into map of string to bool:
    return calling map_from_lists with ks, vs


# --- Embedded C bridges (`antiquus`) ----------------------------------------

@export("atlas__atlas_cmp_i32")
## Compares two `int32_t` cells for `qsort`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `qsort` needs a C callback and the `int32_t` comparison is the branch-free
## `(x > y) - (x < y)`; expressing the byte offsets in PenguScript would cost one
## slice per comparison. It carries `@export` so dead-code elimination keeps it:
## nothing in PenguScript references a function only raw C calls.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads the two borrowed cells; allocates nothing and frees nothing.
antiquus _atlas_cmp_i32 with a as ref to frozen void, b as ref to frozen void into int:
    r"""
int32_t x = *(const int32_t*)a;
int32_t y = *(const int32_t*)b;
return (x > y) - (x < y);
"""

## Sorts an `int` list in place with `qsort` (ascending).
##
## ## Motivo
## The compatibility wrappers (`keys_sorted_ii`, `values_sorted_ii`,
## `keys_sorted_is`) need one C implementation per element type; `qsort` over the
## `PenguList` buffer is faster than the generic insertion sort and reuses the
## same comparator.
##
## ## Memoria
## Sorts the caller's list buffer in place; allocates nothing and frees nothing.
antiquus _atlas_sort_i32_in_place with xs as list of int into void:
    r"""
if (xs.data && xs.len > 1)
qsort(xs.data, (size_t)xs.len, sizeof(int32_t), atlas__atlas_cmp_i32);
"""

@export("atlas__atlas_cmp_f32")
## Compares two `float` cells for `qsort`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `float` is 32-bit, so the comparator dereferences the cells as `const float*`
## and returns `(x > y) - (x < y)`; `NaN` values compare as equal and keep their
## relative order. `@export` keeps it alive through dead-code elimination.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads the two borrowed cells; allocates nothing and frees nothing.
antiquus _atlas_cmp_f32 with a as ref to frozen void, b as ref to frozen void into int:
    r"""
float x = *(const float*)a;
float y = *(const float*)b;
return (x > y) - (x < y);
"""

## Sorts a `float` list in place with `qsort` (ascending).
##
## ## Motivo
## `values_sorted_sf` needs the 32-bit element size (`sizeof(float)`); the
## generic insertion sort would call the `Ordered` bind once per comparison.
##
## ## Memoria
## Sorts the caller's list buffer in place; allocates nothing and frees nothing.
antiquus _atlas_sort_f32_in_place with xs as list of float into void:
    r"""
if (xs.data && xs.len > 1)
qsort(xs.data, (size_t)xs.len, sizeof(float), atlas__atlas_cmp_f32);
"""

@export("atlas__atlas_cmp_string")
## Compares two `PenguString` cells for `qsort` (byte order).
##
## ## Motivo
## `string` has no C ordering operator, so the comparator reads
## `PenguString.data`/`.len` directly: `memcmp` over the common prefix and
## `len` as the tie-breaker, exact for NUL-containing strings and allocation
## free. `@export` keeps it alive through dead-code elimination.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads the two borrowed `PenguString` cells; allocates nothing and frees
## nothing.
antiquus _atlas_cmp_string with a as ref to frozen void, b as ref to frozen void into int:
    r"""
PenguString const *sa = (PenguString const*)a;
PenguString const *sb = (PenguString const*)b;
int n = sa->len < sb->len ? sa->len : sb->len;
int c = memcmp(sa->data, sb->data, (size_t)n);
if (c != 0) return c;
return sa->len - sb->len;
"""

## Sorts a `string` list in place with `qsort` (ascending).
##
## ## Motivo
## `keys_sorted_ss`, `values_sorted_ss`, `values_sorted_is`, `keys_sorted_sf`
## and `_sort_strings` share this one C sort; the element size is the
## `PenguString` cell, not the bytes it points to.
##
## ## Memoria
## Sorts the caller's list buffer in place; the `PenguString` cells are moved,
## not copied, so no string is duplicated or freed.
antiquus _atlas_sort_strings_in_place with xs as list of string into void:
    r"""
if (xs.data && xs.len > 1)
qsort(xs.data, (size_t)xs.len, sizeof(PenguString), atlas__atlas_cmp_string);
"""

# --- Private helpers -------------------------------------------------------

## Sorts a copy of `xs` ascending through the C string comparator.
weave _sort_strings with xs as list of string into list of string:
    var ks as list of string is list of string
    for s in xs:
        calling ks.push with s
    calling _atlas_sort_strings_in_place with ks
    return ks

# --- Tests ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private harness: `std.ward` cannot be imported here (ward imports atlas and
# the cycle would be E0004), so the assertions use `std.spark` directly.
# No fixture type is declared: the custom-key extension (a `seal`/`rune`/
# `alias` plus an UNQUALIFIED `bind <Type> with Ordered:`) is covered by the
# external suite `tests/stdlib/test_atlas.py`, which declares its own
# `seal UserId as int` and `bind UserId with Ordered:` after importing atlas.

## Fails with `label` when `got != want`.
weave _expect_eq_int with got as int, want as int, label as string into void:
    if got != want:
        calling spark.println with "FAIL {label}: got {got}, want {want}"
        calling spark.panic with "atlas: test failed"

## Fails with `label` when `got != want` (compared with `std.scrolls.compare`).
weave _expect_eq_string with got as string, want as string, label as string into void:
    if (calling got.compare with want) != 0:
        calling spark.println with "FAIL {label}: got {got}, want {want}"
        calling spark.panic with "atlas: test failed"

## Fails with `label` when `cond` is false.
weave _expect_true with cond as bool, label as string into void:
    if not cond:
        calling spark.println with "FAIL {label}"
        calling spark.panic with "atlas: test failed"

## Map with the single entry `k -> v` (test helper).
weave _one shard K and V where K: Par, V: Par with k as K, v as V into map of K to V:
    var m as map of K to V is map of K to V
    with m:
        calling .put with k, v
    return m

## Number of elements of `xs` (test helper).
weave _count shard T with xs as list of T into int:
    return calling xs.len

## Fixture `{"alpha": 1, "beta": 2, "gamma": 3}`.
weave _sample_str_int into map of string to int:
    var m as map of string to int is map of string to int
    with m:
        calling .put with "alpha", 1
        calling .put with "beta", 2
        calling .put with "gamma", 3
    return m

